{"summary":"Accept the substantive substrate-model defects: microfauna is missing from the local O2-demand estimate, and heterogeneous-layer porosity is homogenized in a way that can overstate diffusion. Reject the speculative accessor micro-optimization and the stale red-test claim, which does not reproduce in the current workspace.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-1-9df569ce","decision":"accept","rationale":"`effective_substrate_porosity()` reduces a layered bed to a depth-weighted arithmetic mean before squaring it into `D_eff`. For diffusion through stacked media, that lets deep coarse layers offset a restrictive fine cap in a way the transport path does not support, so a low-porosity top layer can indeed make the computed oxic boundary too deep. The exact remedy may vary, but the defect is real."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-a9320302","decision":"reject","rationale":"The repeated computation is real but minor: each accessor does a small scan over the substrate layers, and there is no demonstrated hot-path caller where this is a material cost. The proposed removal or warning does not address a correctness or robustness issue, and even the zone-geometry accessors still recompute the same boundary per call."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-57228e15","decision":"reject","rationale":"I ran `cargo test -p tank_harness --test e2e_geometry_scaling -- --nocapture` in the current workspace and all three tests passed. Because the cited failure does not reproduce here, this amendment does not describe a present defect."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-b43b8059","decision":"accept","rationale":"`estimate_substrate_o2_demand_rate()` only includes decomposer and root demand, even though the bead explicitly defines substrate O2 demand as coming from decomposers, roots, and microfauna. `MicrofaunaState` can still affect penetration indirectly via water-column DO, but the local substrate-demand term is missing a required contributor, so detritivore-heavy substrate activity is underrepresented and penetration depth will be biased too deep."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-0c12a58f","decision":"accept","rationale":"This identifies the same underlying modeling problem as `fr-1-9df569ce`: using a full-depth weighted-average porosity for `D_eff` makes a heterogeneous stack look more diffusive than the shallowest restrictive layer actually allows. That is a real error for layered substrates and can overestimate `o2_penetration_depth_cm`."}]}